{"resourceIdentifier":"5","resourceName":"Greater Lebanon Refuse Authority Landfill Gas Collection and Combustion Project","description":"The “Greater Lebanon Refuse Authority Landfill Flaring and Gas-to-Energy Project” is a two-phased project at the solid waste landfill that serves the communities in Lebanon County, PA. The project benefits climate change strategies by reducing the amount of greenhouse gases (methane) that would otherwise be released from the landfill. The methane is destroyed by combustion in generators or in an enclosed flare.  The project’s first part is a landfill gas capture and flaring operation that came online in July 2002. The second part is a larger landfill gas-to-energy project that came online in September, 2007. The gas-to-energy project consists of gas wells, piping, two 1.6-MW generators, the flare (now for backup purposes), and a Renewable Energy Education Center.","location":{"latitude":40.366200,"longitude":-76.492930},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":null,"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string","value":"5"}]},{"code":"STATE_PROVINCE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"PA"}]}],"participationSummaries":[{"programCode":"VCS","attributes":[{"code":"PROPONENT_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Greater Lebanon Refuse Authority"},{"type":"string","value":"Pennsylvania, United States"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_STATUS","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Registered"},{"type":"assetSearchLink","value":null,"targetId":"5"}]},{"code":"EST_ANNUAL_EMISSION_REDCT","values":[{"type":"string","value":"25600"}]},{"code":"PRIMARY_PROJECT_CATEGORY_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Waste handling and disposal"}]},{"code":"PROTOCOL_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"ACM0001"}]},{"code":"VALIDATOR_NAME","values":[{"type":"string","value":"Tuev Sued Industrie Service GmbH (Tuev Sued)"}]},{"code":"PROJECT_REGISTRATION_DATE","values":[{"type":"string","value":"06/04/2020"}]},{"code":"CREDIT_PE